WEBVTT

00:05.005 --> 00:07.924
TOKYO PREFECTURAL JUJUTSU HIGH SCHOOL

00:08.508 --> 00:10.385
Here we go.

00:13.346 --> 00:16.433
Can't we have more vending machines?

00:17.100 --> 00:20.603
No way, not many can enter
this school anyway.

00:20.687 --> 00:22.188
What?

00:22.272 --> 00:24.357
Where are the first-year students?

00:24.441 --> 00:25.734
I sent them on an errand.

00:25.817 --> 00:26.943
Bonito flakes.

00:27.527 --> 00:29.237
-Will it be okay?
-Salmon.

00:29.821 --> 00:33.241
They are not three-year-old kids.
They know how to run errands.

00:33.324 --> 00:35.326
That's not what I meant.

00:35.827 --> 00:38.955
Isn't the principal of
Kyoto Jujutsu High School coming today?

00:39.039 --> 00:39.956
What?

00:40.540 --> 00:42.459
The meeting for the Goodwill Event.

00:44.252 --> 00:47.380
That abnormal case where
the first-year students were dispatched.

00:47.464 --> 00:51.176
Wasn't it done by the higher-ups
who have a tense relationship with Satoru?

00:52.135 --> 00:55.722
The principal of Kyoto
is part of the higher-ups, right?

00:55.805 --> 00:58.058
If they bump into each other…

00:58.933 --> 01:02.979
Itadori, the first-year student
they targeted, is dead.

01:03.521 --> 01:06.566
They probably don't plan
to do anything to Megumi and Kugisaki.

01:08.109 --> 01:10.028
Even the old man in Kyoto

01:10.570 --> 01:13.239
won't cause trouble,
at least on the surface.

01:13.323 --> 01:14.574
Salmon.

01:15.617 --> 01:17.786
The teachers may have
their own standpoints,

01:17.869 --> 01:19.913
but not necessarily the students.

01:19.996 --> 01:22.832
Do you mean Mai is here?

01:23.416 --> 01:24.751
It's just my guess.

01:24.834 --> 01:27.796
After all, the meeting
has nothing to do with the students.

01:29.088 --> 01:30.799
However…

01:31.758 --> 01:34.594
Don't they like to harass people?

01:35.303 --> 01:37.013
Todo and Mai.

01:37.680 --> 01:40.475
Why are you here, Zenin?

01:40.558 --> 01:41.935
Oh, I knew it.

01:42.519 --> 01:45.021
She gives off a similar vibe.
Are they sisters?

01:45.104 --> 01:46.272
They are twins.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.983
Gosh, Fushiguro.

01:49.067 --> 01:51.653
If you call me that,
it will be the same as Maki.

01:52.695 --> 01:54.531
Call me "Mai."

01:54.614 --> 01:58.159
These two are the substitutes for Okkotsu
and the third-year students?

01:58.243 --> 02:01.830
We followed the principal here
because we were worried about you.

02:01.913 --> 02:04.165
Your classmate died, right?

02:04.249 --> 02:07.669
Are you sad? Or maybe not?

02:09.087 --> 02:10.839
What are you trying to say?

02:10.922 --> 02:12.340
It's okay.

02:12.423 --> 02:14.717
There are things that can be hard to say.

02:14.801 --> 02:16.719
I'll say it on your behalf instead.

02:16.803 --> 02:19.305
The term "vessel" sounds good,

02:19.389 --> 02:22.142
but to speak crudely,
he's just a half-cursed monster, right?

02:23.184 --> 02:26.187
Such a dirty and inhuman thing.

02:26.271 --> 02:29.023
Yet he calls himself
a Jujutsu Sorcerer, like you.

02:29.107 --> 02:30.942
He must have made you disgusted.

02:31.609 --> 02:34.445
Isn't it good riddance that he's dead?

02:37.031 --> 02:40.577
Mai, stop talking about useless stuff.

02:41.244 --> 02:44.247
I only want to know

02:44.330 --> 02:46.541
if they are good enough
to replace Okkotsu.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.544
That's all!

02:51.337 --> 02:53.423
Your name is Fushiguro, right?

02:54.424 --> 02:56.551
What kind of woman do you like?

02:57.969 --> 02:59.220
-What?
-What?

02:59.846 --> 03:04.225
Based on your answer, I might beat you up
until you're half dead right here.

03:04.809 --> 03:06.185
Okkotsu…

03:06.269 --> 03:09.981
At worst, I'll drag the third-year
students to the Goodwill Event.

03:12.317 --> 03:13.902
By the way…

03:14.944 --> 03:18.615
I like tall women with big butts!

04:53.626 --> 04:55.712
I just met you for the first time today.

04:55.795 --> 04:58.506
Why should I tell you
about the kind of girl I like?

04:58.589 --> 04:59.882
What?

04:59.966 --> 05:02.844
Yes, you're making things difficult
for this boring man.

05:02.927 --> 05:04.595
Shut up.

05:04.679 --> 05:07.890
The situation is already weird enough.
Stop making it worse.

05:08.558 --> 05:11.644
I'm Aoi Todo, a third-year student
at Kyoto Jujutsu High School.

05:11.728 --> 05:13.521
That's all for my self-introduction.

05:13.604 --> 05:15.315
We're friends now.

05:15.398 --> 05:18.067
Hurry up and answer.
It's okay if it's a man.

05:19.110 --> 05:22.697
Sexual preferences
can reflect one's personality.

05:22.780 --> 05:26.826
Someone who has boring tastes
in women is boring!

05:28.411 --> 05:31.789
I hate boring men the most!

05:32.790 --> 05:37.795
The Goodwill Event is a special show
for me to show my passion and soul.

05:37.879 --> 05:41.674
If you make me bored
in my last Goodwill Event,

05:41.758 --> 05:44.302
I don't know what's going to happen.

05:44.385 --> 05:47.346
Hey. Jujutsu high schools
adopt a four-year program, right?

05:47.430 --> 05:49.932
You can only participate
until your third year.

05:50.016 --> 05:51.559
I see.

05:52.268 --> 05:55.855
As a form of consideration,
I can still leave you half dead.

05:55.938 --> 05:59.233
Answer me, Fushiguro.
What kind of woman do you like?

05:59.317 --> 06:01.069
What's this? A variety show?

06:02.028 --> 06:03.988
Is that a summer uniform?

06:04.572 --> 06:06.741
I'm annoyed, but I'm jealous.

06:07.408 --> 06:09.243
Kugisaki's unarmed right now.

06:09.327 --> 06:10.995
We need to avoid a fight.

06:12.914 --> 06:15.750
It's not a bad thing
to be unable to forgive someone.

06:15.833 --> 06:18.211
Isn't that part of your kindness too?

06:20.671 --> 06:23.466
I don't have any preferences.

06:24.133 --> 06:26.844
As long as she isn't easily swayed,

06:26.928 --> 06:28.971
I don't ask for anything else.

06:31.390 --> 06:33.434
That's a good answer.

06:33.518 --> 06:36.354
I would kill him if he said
he likes big breasts or something.

06:36.938 --> 06:38.147
Shut up.

06:39.774 --> 06:41.359
I knew it.

06:43.194 --> 06:46.781
You're so boring, Fushiguro.

06:54.455 --> 06:55.289
Fushiguro!

06:56.374 --> 06:59.836
Oh, man. I feel so bad for Fushiguro.

07:01.420 --> 07:04.966
He's a genius who enrolled
as a Grade 2 Jujutsu Sorcerer,

07:05.049 --> 07:09.470
and yet he's nothing but a first-year
in front of our Grade 1 Todo.

07:09.554 --> 07:12.473
I should console him later.

07:13.099 --> 07:15.935
I thought you two are alike,
but I was wrong.

07:16.644 --> 07:19.313
Maki's a hundred times
more beautiful than you.

07:20.481 --> 07:23.568
Do you lack sleep? Your pores are huge.

07:25.445 --> 07:27.155
I'll teach you…

07:28.656 --> 07:30.658
how to talk nicely.

07:34.245 --> 07:37.123
I knew it when I first saw you.

07:37.623 --> 07:39.917
"This guy is so boring."

07:40.418 --> 07:43.963
However,
I can't judge a book by its cover.

07:44.547 --> 07:47.383
That's why I asked.

07:48.426 --> 07:51.846
But you trampled on my kindness.

07:52.638 --> 07:55.892
Don't tell me
your brain's made of pineapple, too.

07:57.477 --> 07:58.811
Todo?

07:58.895 --> 08:00.813
Is he that Todo?

08:01.689 --> 08:02.899
Last year,

08:02.982 --> 08:06.152
Geto started an unprecedented
cursed technique terrorist attack.

08:06.235 --> 08:09.030
During the Shinjuku-to-Kyoto
Night Line of a Hundred Demons,

08:09.655 --> 08:12.533
he exorcised five Grade 1 Cursed Spirits

08:12.617 --> 08:15.745
and one Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

08:16.370 --> 08:17.747
He's that Todo?

08:18.247 --> 08:21.792
But it's not unusual for a Grade 1
Sorcerer to defeat a Special Grade.

08:22.293 --> 08:23.753
What's amazing is that…

08:24.337 --> 08:26.923
I heard you don't use cursed techniques.

08:27.006 --> 08:28.090
What?

08:28.174 --> 08:30.676
Oh, that rumor is fake.

08:31.344 --> 08:33.179
I used it against a Special Grade.

08:33.262 --> 08:36.432
You don't use it on Grade 1 Curses?
What a monster!

08:36.516 --> 08:38.559
I'm so relieved.

08:39.685 --> 08:40.728
Nue…

08:42.522 --> 08:43.689
and Toad.

08:48.152 --> 08:49.570
The Well's Unknown Abyss.

08:53.074 --> 08:54.033
What?

08:54.116 --> 08:56.327
The opponent focuses
on close-range combat.

08:56.410 --> 08:59.038
I need to put some distance between us
and move in quickly.

09:03.960 --> 09:06.671
He's quick! That was not his full speed--

09:06.754 --> 09:09.173
You're too shallow.

09:09.257 --> 09:14.387
Your physique is thin
and your preferences are equally shallow!

09:27.358 --> 09:30.319
Darn it! He's too strong!

09:41.831 --> 09:45.418
It's not over yet!

09:53.342 --> 09:55.261
It's always the same.

09:55.344 --> 09:56.971
This is too boring!

10:07.523 --> 10:10.860
I don't sense any enthusiasm in you.

10:11.360 --> 10:14.113
I was just being nice,
and you're acting all high-and-mighty.

10:14.196 --> 10:16.574
Since you said that…

10:19.201 --> 10:20.661
Then I'll do it.

10:23.831 --> 10:25.082
Bring it on!

10:26.417 --> 10:27.418
Don't move.

10:30.296 --> 10:33.883
What are you doing?

10:36.677 --> 10:39.221
We barely made it.

10:39.305 --> 10:40.765
Bonito flakes.

10:43.434 --> 10:45.853
But to be honest, I was late.

10:47.688 --> 10:50.191
Long time no see, Panda.

10:50.274 --> 10:53.110
Why can't you wait
until the Goodwill Event?

10:53.194 --> 10:54.445
Go back.

10:54.528 --> 10:55.863
Or I'll scream.

10:55.946 --> 10:57.406
"Don't!"

10:57.490 --> 10:59.742
No need to tell me. I'm going back.

11:00.242 --> 11:01.911
Where's my shirt?

11:04.413 --> 11:07.833
Seems like it won't be that boring
the entire time.

11:07.917 --> 11:09.126
What?

11:10.419 --> 11:14.590
Tell Okkotsu that
he has to attend the event as well.

11:15.174 --> 11:16.300
It's troublesome.

11:16.384 --> 11:19.303
I'm a panda.
I don't understand human language.

11:19.387 --> 11:20.596
Salmon.

11:26.310 --> 11:28.229
If you still want to be
a Jujutsu Sorcerer,

11:28.312 --> 11:30.731
you should learn to pick your opponent.

11:34.860 --> 11:38.239
What are you doing to my gofer, Mai?

11:38.322 --> 11:39.281
Oh, my.

11:39.365 --> 11:43.160
You look so much like a loser
that I didn't realize it was you, Maki.

11:43.244 --> 11:45.663
The same goes for you.

11:45.746 --> 11:48.833
You also only know
how to inject cursed energy into tools.

11:48.916 --> 11:50.876
As if you know crap
about cursed techniques.

11:50.960 --> 11:53.129
It's better than
having no cursed energy at all.

11:53.212 --> 11:55.631
Your neck will feel sore
if you always look up.

11:55.714 --> 11:57.967
Sometimes, you need to look down too.

11:58.050 --> 12:02.304
Forget it. It's a disgrace
to be arguing among losers.

12:02.847 --> 12:04.557
Can you stand, Nobara?

12:04.640 --> 12:07.685
No way. She's not getting up for a while.

12:07.768 --> 12:09.603
I taught her a lesson--

12:10.771 --> 12:13.149
What's this? Are you going to fight?

12:16.819 --> 12:19.029
Nice support, Maki!

12:20.573 --> 12:23.534
How dare you open so many holes
in the sportswear I just bought!

12:23.617 --> 12:27.371
Give me your uniform.
I'll make that my summer uniform!

12:28.038 --> 12:31.208
Next time, I'll add a few holes
to your body.

12:31.292 --> 12:34.712
Besides, you can't wear it
with your short legs--

12:37.339 --> 12:39.049
I'm killing you!

12:39.550 --> 12:41.302
Let's go back, Mai.

12:42.678 --> 12:45.097
No way…

12:45.181 --> 12:47.183
My shirt's here.

12:47.975 --> 12:49.518
Where's Fushiguro?

12:49.602 --> 12:52.354
Don't worry.
Panda and Inumaki went to help him.

12:52.438 --> 12:54.398
Looks fun here.

12:55.566 --> 12:58.569
Are you serious? I'm just about to start.

12:58.652 --> 12:59.570
You can't.

12:59.653 --> 13:03.324
Unlike you,
I have something important to do in Tokyo.

13:04.617 --> 13:06.285
There's an…

13:07.036 --> 13:08.829
individual handshake event with Takada!

13:08.913 --> 13:10.789
TAKADA THE TALL IDOL

13:12.166 --> 13:13.792
-What?
-I see.

13:17.129 --> 13:19.882
If I can't get to the venue in time,

13:19.965 --> 13:22.259
there's no telling what I'm going to do.

13:23.135 --> 13:25.179
Come with me, Mai!

13:25.262 --> 13:27.640
Gosh! What a selfish person!

13:29.433 --> 13:32.436
To think that she skipped
the usual Kyoto for her tour.

13:32.520 --> 13:35.898
Listen, it won't end so easily
during the Goodwill Event.

13:35.981 --> 13:38.317
Why are you acting like you won?

13:38.400 --> 13:40.486
Leave your uniform behind!

13:40.569 --> 13:42.071
Stop it, you fool.

13:42.154 --> 13:44.823
It brings no benefit to win or lose here.

13:44.907 --> 13:46.992
We'll finish them at the Goodwill Event.

13:48.494 --> 13:49.870
Hey, Maki.

13:49.954 --> 13:53.123
Is it true that you have no cursed energy?

13:53.916 --> 13:55.376
Yes.

13:55.459 --> 13:56.544
That's why…

13:57.461 --> 14:00.214
Without these glasses,
I can't even see curses.

14:00.798 --> 14:02.633
What I use is called a Cursed Tool.

14:02.716 --> 14:04.885
It's a tool that's imbued with a curse.

14:05.386 --> 14:08.013
Unlike you guys,
I don't use my own cursed energy

14:08.097 --> 14:09.765
to use sorcery and techniques.

14:12.184 --> 14:14.603
Is it the same as Itadori's knife?

14:16.438 --> 14:18.649
Then why did you become
a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

14:20.025 --> 14:21.360
I acted in a fit of pique.

14:22.695 --> 14:26.365
If I, who have been looked down upon,
become a great Jujutsu Sorcerer,

14:26.448 --> 14:29.076
I wonder how
my family members would react?

14:29.159 --> 14:30.369
I can't wait to see that.

14:32.246 --> 14:34.874
Come on. Let's go to Ms. Shoko.

14:38.419 --> 14:41.213
I respect you very much, Maki!

14:41.714 --> 14:42.882
Oh, really?

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.105
Is Yaga still not here?

00:15:08.731 --> 00:15:10.774
As an old man with my days numbered,

00:15:10.858 --> 00:15:12.610
my time is precious.

00:15:16.614 --> 00:15:19.074
Principal Yaga won't be coming
for a while.

00:15:20.326 --> 00:15:21.493
Really?

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:27.499
Since I gave him a fake meeting time…

00:15:27.583 --> 00:15:29.752
…by threatening Ijichi.

00:15:30.586 --> 00:15:33.964
I've been under your care,
Principal Gakuganji.

00:15:34.465 --> 00:15:37.092
Let's see. What do you mean by that?

00:15:37.176 --> 00:15:39.011
Don't act dumb, old man.

00:15:39.094 --> 00:15:41.055
It's about Itadori.

00:15:41.138 --> 00:15:44.391
You're involved in it since you are
the head of the conservative, right?

00:15:46.936 --> 00:15:48.437
Dear me.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.650
Youngsters nowadays
can't even speak with respect?

00:15:53.233 --> 00:15:55.611
I don't intend to respect you
from the beginning.

00:15:55.694 --> 00:15:59.365
Old people nowadays are too arrogant,
it's really a pain in the butt.

00:15:59.448 --> 00:16:01.367
-Hey.
-What?

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.535
This is problematic behavior.

00:16:03.619 --> 00:16:06.747
We'll report it
to the relevant department.

00:16:07.915 --> 00:16:12.044
Oh, my goodness!
It's Satoru Gojo in person!

00:16:12.127 --> 00:16:16.340
Please help yourself.
I don't intend to stay for long.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.886
He talked to me!

00:16:23.138 --> 00:16:26.976
Last night, I was attacked by two
unregistered Special Grade Cursed Spirits.

00:16:27.059 --> 00:16:28.394
Is that so?

00:16:28.477 --> 00:16:30.688
That's unfortunate.

00:16:31.271 --> 00:16:32.940
Don't be mistaken.

00:16:33.023 --> 00:16:36.694
To me, it's almost like
the usual street interview.

00:16:38.278 --> 00:16:40.322
He's so cool!

00:16:41.323 --> 00:16:47.121
Those Cursed Spirits can communicate.
They must have comrades of the same level.

00:16:49.832 --> 00:16:51.709
It's not just our enemies.

00:16:51.792 --> 00:16:54.628
Hakari, Okkotsu, and your Todo.

00:16:55.337 --> 00:16:59.133
In recent years, the level of students
has also improved by leaps and bounds.

00:17:00.426 --> 00:17:03.804
Also, we had
the Suguru Geto incident last year.

00:17:07.349 --> 00:17:10.477
And now,
the appearance of Sukuna's vessel.

00:17:11.478 --> 00:17:13.564
What are you trying to say?

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.858
Don't you get it?

00:17:15.941 --> 00:17:20.988
The power you suppressed
for lame status and tradition

00:17:21.071 --> 00:17:24.283
has begun to grow and surge.

00:17:24.992 --> 00:17:29.246
"Special Grade" will no longer be
the ceiling for the future generation.

00:17:29.872 --> 00:17:32.791
If you think I'm the only one
who will bare my fangs at you,

00:17:32.875 --> 00:17:35.753
then you're in for a ride, old man.

00:17:36.336 --> 00:17:40.758
You're talking a little too much.

00:17:40.841 --> 00:17:42.760
So frightening.

00:17:42.843 --> 00:17:46.305
I've said everything that I wanted.
I should leave now.

00:17:51.435 --> 00:17:55.647
By the way, Principal Yaga
will be here in two hours. Bye!

00:17:56.231 --> 00:17:57.649
Two hours?

00:18:01.737 --> 00:18:05.657
-Go get me some tea, Miwa.
-Yes, sir.

00:18:09.745 --> 00:18:11.121
Please excuse me.

00:18:16.293 --> 00:18:19.254
If I catch up,
I'll ask to take a photo with him!

00:18:19.338 --> 00:18:22.257
TAKADA'S INDIVIDUAL HANDSHAKE EVENT

00:18:24.301 --> 00:18:27.346
Please do the Takada's beam once.

00:18:27.429 --> 00:18:30.307
Okay, I'll do it now.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.435
Tantaka-tan!

00:18:37.314 --> 00:18:39.024
Time's up.

00:18:40.442 --> 00:18:43.737
ONE MONTH LATER

00:18:44.321 --> 00:18:45.489
RECORD - SEPTEMBER 2018

00:18:45.572 --> 00:18:47.866
KINEMA CINEMA
KAWASAKI, KANAGAWA PREFECTURE

00:19:11.056 --> 00:19:12.474
AFTER THE MOVIE SCREENING,

00:19:12.558 --> 00:19:16.103
A STAFF DISCOVERED THREE
PECULIAR BODIES OF HIGH-SCHOOL STUDENTS

00:19:16.186 --> 00:19:19.481
CAUSE OF DEATH: INCREASED INTRACRANIAL
PRESSURE AND RESPIRATION PARALYSIS

00:19:19.565 --> 00:19:20.983
AS A RESULT OF HEAD DEFORMATION

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.413
Excuse me.

00:19:37.124 --> 00:19:38.542
The incident in the cinema…

00:19:40.377 --> 00:19:42.087
Did you do it?

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:49.595
Wow. So you can see me.

00:20:02.065 --> 00:20:03.400
KINEMA CINEMA

00:20:03.483 --> 00:20:05.110
It's a horrifying crime scene.

00:20:06.278 --> 00:20:08.989
Are you prepared, Itadori?

00:20:12.701 --> 00:20:13.619
Yes.

00:21:53.468 --> 00:21:54.886
Thank you!

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:56.596
No problem.

00:21:57.306 --> 00:21:59.391
I got it!

00:22:13.196 --> 00:22:14.281
Where's my tea?

00:22:14.364 --> 00:22:15.365
Oh, god.

00:22:16.033 --> 00:22:18.452
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

00:22:18.535 --> 00:22:19.995
INDIVIDUAL HANDSHAKE EVENT VENUE

00:22:21.538 --> 00:22:24.833
There's a beautiful woman
looking at us like trash.

00:22:24.916 --> 00:22:26.209
Don't get too excited.

00:22:26.293 --> 00:22:28.211
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mai.

00:22:28.295 --> 00:22:30.881
What's wrong? Did something bad happen?

00:22:30.964 --> 00:22:32.966
Ask yourself.

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:35.052
Is the moment finally here?

00:22:35.135 --> 00:22:35.969
What?

00:22:36.053 --> 00:22:37.471
What's this?

00:22:37.554 --> 00:22:39.473
The next handshake event.

00:22:39.556 --> 00:22:42.851
You should go feel
Takada's beauty in person.

00:22:42.934 --> 00:22:44.686
It's troublesome.

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:48.690
This is also a fan
and a future husband's duty.

00:22:48.774 --> 00:22:50.609
How disgusting.

00:22:50.692 --> 00:22:54.613
But it will be more troublesome
if I refuse it.

00:22:54.696 --> 00:22:55.864
What's wrong?

00:23:00.952 --> 00:23:02.370
I get it.

00:23:03.663 --> 00:23:04.873
What?

00:23:06.249 --> 00:23:07.959
It's a girl!

00:23:08.043 --> 00:23:09.795
Is this your first time?

00:23:09.878 --> 00:23:10.879
Yes.

00:23:10.962 --> 00:23:12.714
What's your name?

00:23:12.798 --> 00:23:13.840
Mai.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:18.553
Mai, are you tired?
Was it tiring to wait in line?

00:23:18.637 --> 00:23:21.389
I'm tired of people,
rather than the waiting.

00:23:21.473 --> 00:23:24.851
You should come again
when you feel better.

00:23:24.935 --> 00:23:27.395
I'll remember you, Mai.

00:23:28.271 --> 00:23:29.898
You're back, Mai.

00:23:30.482 --> 00:23:31.441
How was it?

00:23:31.942 --> 00:23:32.901
Nothing special.

00:23:34.361 --> 00:23:38.865
Takada is indeed a woman
who can't be easily described in words.

00:23:41.993 --> 00:23:45.914
That wasn't all too bad.
